# 03 -- derivative-free local search (NLOPT:LN_SBPLX).
#
# When gradients are unreliable (noisy LAMMPS loss components),
# a derivative-free local optimiser is more robust than BFGS.
# LN_SBPLX is a Subplex variant of Nelder-Mead.
#
# STEP is the initial step as a FRACTION of each OPTIM width (0 < STEP
# <= 0.5): 0.1 here means 10% of [4,6] on RCUT2B and 10% of [0.1,0.4]
# on SGRIDMB -- the "one tenth of the expected change" rule of thumb.
# hpo_run.log prints the effective per-dimension step.

OPTIMIZER
  STRATEGY
    TYPE PLAIN
    LIB NLOPT
    ALGO LN_SBPLX
    MAXEVAL 60
    STEP 0.1
  ENDSTRATEGY
ENDOPTIMIZER

LOSS L2
FAILSCORE 1e16
PC_ERMSE 0 0.0001
PC_LAMMPS --script ../common/lammps/Ecoh.in --hotvar hot_a0 2.5 4.5 3.302 --varloss Ecoh 8.10 800

OPTIM RCUT2B  (1) 4.0 6.0
OPTIM SGRIDMB (1) 0.1 0.4

OUTPUT 1
BOUTPUT 1
